WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
People are going to have to start

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.820
paying their fair share in taxes.

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.500
Their “fair share?”

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.620
Are you paying your fair share?

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.020
What would that be?

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.740
Do you have a specific on the tax rate?

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:13.540
You know, you look at our tax rates back in the ‘60s

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.660
STOSSEL: On 60 minutes,

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.900
the darling of the progressive movement,

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.760
didn’t appear to have a specific rate in mind

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.200
but then she said…

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.720
Ocasio-Cortez: Sometimes you see tax rates

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.060
as high as 60 or 70%.

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.920
STOSSEL: Suddenly that became the progressive plan.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.620
I can support folks at the top paying their fair share.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.760
70 percent, 80 percent, we’ve had it as high as 90 percent

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.040
STOSSEL: 90% was the top tax rate when I was a kid

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.600
and now democrats say,

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.980
“if we just raise rates on the wealthy,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.220
government will have plenty of money

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.300
to pay for all their wonderful programs.”

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.060
[sound of money counting]

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:50.660
But it’s a myth.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.220
What progressives don’t say is that:

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.420
No one actually paid anywhere close to those rates.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.240
No one?

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.060
No one.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.660
Economic historian Phillip Magness says

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:02.000
it’s not surprising that progressives don’t know that

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.530
90% tax rates didn’t bring in lots of money.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.960
You know, who has the time and the interest

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.820
to sit around and dig through that line by line?

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:10.720
You.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:12.080
Me. I'm apparently the guy.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.500
He's researched old tax codes for over a decade.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.340
You must be a really boring guy.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.060
I can be.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.860
[Sound of plane engine ]

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.400
During World War II, America’s 90% tax bracket

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.260
didn’t bring in that much more money

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:29.140
because rich people found loopholes.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:31.580
And then, because the high rates discouraged work

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.630
President Kennedy backed a bill that

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:36.020
lowered the top rate to 70%.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.380
President Kennedy: The billions of dollars

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.920
this bill would place in the hands of the consumer

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.200
and our businessmen

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.700
will have both immediate and permanent benefits

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.120
to our economy.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.420
[applause]

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:50.400
STOSSEL: But it turned out that the 70% rate

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.300
wasn’t very real either.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.660
No one paid 70%, let alone 90%?

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.660
Right.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:57.670
What did they pay?

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:00.060
A millionaire on average would pay 41%

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.240
Because when taxes are high, rich people find loopholes.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.720
There’s all these deductions and exemptions

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.860
and carve outs that are intentionally baked

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.240
into the tax code.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.920
Newspapers ran ads:

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:13.760
"Cruise for free!"

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.380
$2499 value.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.020
Basically take a vacation around the Caribbean,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.380
but while you're onboard the ship you attend say,

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.700
an investing seminar or a real estate seminar

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.260
then write off the trip.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.040
The whole trip?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:27.660
The whole trip.

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.340
Deductions became so complex

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.580
that rich people,

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.780
instead of inventing, say a precursor to the iPhone,

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.980
hired accountants to study the tax code.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.940
Who can afford the best accountants?

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.120
It's always the wealthy.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:43.340
STOSSEL: Today the top tax rate is 37%.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.740
The top rate started dropping again after

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.340
Ronald Reagan said 70% was outrageous:

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.580
President Reagan: Our tax system

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:52.700
could only be described as un-American.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.820
And the democrats actually agree with him.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.060
Reagan goes to the table and says, "Let's make a deal."

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.940
We can cut the rates down to something

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.980
closer in approximation to what we have today

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.540
and in exchange we'll consolidate the tax code.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:08.400
Vacation deductions and other exemptions were killed,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.420
leading to a slightly simpler tax code

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.520
and surprise, the lower rates brought in

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.180
just as much money.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.080
Turns out that tax revenue as a

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.820
percentage of the economy

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.300
stays about the same

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.660
no matter what the top tax rate is.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.400
When rates are high, rich people sometimes work less.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.140
It’s just economics.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.200
People don’t work to pay taxes.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.840
Economist Art Laffer told president Reagan

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.120
rich people will evade high taxes.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.080
They’ll change where they earn their income.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.409
They’ll change how they earn their income.

00:03:40.409 --> 00:03:41.980
They’ll change how much they earn,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.380
when they receive the income.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:46.700
They’ll change all of those things to minimize taxes.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.580
They will leave the United States.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.520
And this not-yet-president pointed out that

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.560
if taxes go up, rich people may move away.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.740
You haven’t left.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.920
I haven’t left yet.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.220
Are you going to leave?

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:59.360
Big story if I leave, I guess.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.960
If I leave New York that’s a big story.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.480
Look, the rich people are going to leave.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.980
And other people are going to leave.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.200
You're going to end up with lots of people

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.360
that don’t produce.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.580
And then,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.860
that’s the spiral that’s the end.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.440
That's what's happened and

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.200
there's some European examples.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.940
So France attempted a massive tax

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:17.860
on its wealthiest earners.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.300
What they found is the business people

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.440
left in a mass exodus from the country.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.500
But progressives are selective when they look at history

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.740
Under republican president, republican administration,

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.760
Dwight Eisenhower we had 90% marginal tax rates.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.760
The government will collect more and do good things.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:36.980
Well, that's the claim.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.280
But you're asking for an economic disaster.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:40.480
So I ask the question,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.020
do we leave it in the private sector

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.280
where the market decides?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.140
Or do we subject it to corrupt politicians?

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.840
I say, let the market decide.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.480
Of course, when the market decides,

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.900
some people get really rich.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.780
STOSSEL: And then progressives say:

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:57.700
Sen. Sanders: The rich get richer and the poor get poorer.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.340
But it’s not true.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.380
The poor don’t get poorer.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.640
That’s another economic myth.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.300
We will cover that, in an upcoming video.

